1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,783
Last class, everything on your map was on one side. Yours.

2
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:07,407
Today the map gets politics.

3
00:00:07,857 --> 00:00:10,030
These people want your hulk.

4
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:13,089
These people will fix your ship.

5
00:00:13,539 --> 00:00:20,496
That is two records in your file, and one line that says who is whose enemy.

6
00:00:21,696 --> 00:00:25,174
You read these three lines in Lecture 11.

7
00:00:25,624 --> 00:00:31,711
They make a side called tsn, and give it a name and a color.

8
00:00:32,161 --> 00:00:35,204
Look where else that word turns up.

9
00:00:35,654 --> 00:00:37,393
DS 1: tsn, station.

10
00:00:37,843 --> 00:00:39,583
The hulk: tsn, derelict.

11
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:41,772
Your tug: tsn, tug.

12
00:00:42,222 --> 00:00:46,570
Inside the quote marks, the first word is the side.

13
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,759
The rest are roles.

14
00:00:49,209 --> 00:00:52,687
The crew's own ship is on tsn too.

15
00:00:53,137 --> 00:00:57,050
So tsn is the key of your own side.

16
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:59,674
Hold on to that word.

17
00:01:00,874 --> 00:01:03,483
Sides are records, like everything else.

18
00:01:03,933 --> 00:01:08,715
A section: two hashes, Sides, and the key is sides, exactly.

19
00:01:09,165 --> 00:01:13,948
One record for a side: three hashes, a name, a key.

20
00:01:14,398 --> 00:01:22,659
My own side goes first, and its key is tsn, because that is the word my ship already carries.

21
00:01:23,109 --> 00:01:27,891
A color: hash, then three characters, for red, green and blue.

22
00:01:28,341 --> 00:01:30,950
Zero is none, F is all.

23
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:34,878
And a line about who they are. Lint.

24
00:01:35,328 --> 00:01:39,241
Nothing in this mission reads a section keyed sides.

25
00:01:39,691 --> 00:01:47,952
And lint is right: the script has a line for quests, a line for scans, a line for landmarks.

26
00:01:48,402 --> 00:01:50,141
Nothing for sides. Yet.

27
00:01:51,341 --> 00:01:56,124
One card today, and there is nothing on it to change.

28
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:58,748
Line 35 reads my file.

29
00:01:59,198 --> 00:02:08,328
I go to the end of that line, press Enter twice, and type two lines, lined up with it. A note.

30
00:02:08,778 --> 00:02:13,561
And the line: make the sides, from the section called sides.

31
00:02:14,011 --> 00:02:18,793
It is the same shape as the landmarks line further down.

32
00:02:19,243 --> 00:02:20,983
Where it goes matters.

33
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:26,215
Below line 35, because line 35 is what reads the file.

34
00:02:26,665 --> 00:02:34,491
And four spaces in, above the arrow END, so it is one of the map's lines. Both checks.

35
00:02:34,941 --> 00:02:36,246
Clean, and nothing.

36
00:02:37,446 --> 00:02:42,663
Now the people who are not me. The Breakers. Key, breaker. Orange.

37
00:02:43,113 --> 00:02:46,157
And the line that matters: Enemies, tsn.

38
00:02:46,607 --> 00:02:50,085
The Harbor Guild. Key, guild. Green. Allies, tsn.

39
00:02:50,535 --> 00:02:54,448
After the colon comes a key, never a name.

40
00:02:54,898 --> 00:02:57,072
And I say it once.

41
00:02:57,522 --> 00:03:03,174
Enemies tsn on the Breakers makes them my enemy and makes me theirs.

42
00:03:03,624 --> 00:03:08,841
I do not go back and write it on my own record.

43
00:03:10,041 --> 00:03:15,259
A side with nothing on it is a name in a file.

44
00:03:15,709 --> 00:03:17,013
So, two landmarks.

45
00:03:17,463 --> 00:03:20,072
A ship: kind npc, side breaker.

46
00:03:20,522 --> 00:03:22,261
Out past the hulk.

47
00:03:22,711 --> 00:03:24,450
A station: side guild.

48
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:26,639
West of DS 1.

49
00:03:27,089 --> 00:03:29,698
The Side line takes the key.

50
00:03:30,148 --> 00:03:32,322
Watch where I am typing.

51
00:03:32,772 --> 00:03:37,120
These go in the Landmarks section, above the Sides heading.

52
00:03:37,570 --> 00:03:47,135
Type a landmark below that heading and the game reads it as a side called Breaker Cutter, and puts no ship anywhere.

53
00:03:48,335 --> 00:03:51,378
Lecture 10 warned you about this one.

54
00:03:51,828 --> 00:03:54,437
My story ends with: reach station.

55
00:03:54,887 --> 00:03:58,800
Station is a role, and every station wears it.

56
00:03:59,250 --> 00:04:02,293
I have just built a second station.

57
00:04:02,743 --> 00:04:07,526
The crew could carry the log to the Guild and win.

58
00:04:07,976 --> 00:04:11,889
So DS 1 gets a role of its own.

59
00:04:12,339 --> 00:04:14,513
In the step: reach home.

60
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:18,876
Lint says nothing wears a role called home. True.

61
00:04:19,326 --> 00:04:22,804
So, line 62, where DS 1 is made.

62
00:04:23,254 --> 00:04:27,167
Inside the quote marks, after station: comma, space, home.

63
00:04:27,617 --> 00:04:29,791
Side first, then roles. Clean.

64
00:04:30,991 --> 00:04:32,730
Three sides, three pairs.

65
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:35,354
Me and the Breakers: enemies.

66
00:04:35,804 --> 00:04:37,978
Me and the Guild: allies.

67
00:04:38,428 --> 00:04:41,472
The Breakers and the Guild: nobody said.

68
00:04:41,922 --> 00:04:46,270
And a pair nobody mentions is nothing to each other.

69
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:48,893
The game does not guess.

70
00:04:49,343 --> 00:04:54,561
Scavengers and harbor pilots are not strangers, so: Enemies, tsn, comma, guild.

71
00:04:55,011 --> 00:04:57,620
What does a relation buy you?

72
00:04:58,070 --> 00:05:03,722
An enemy reads as an enemy on Science, and Comms can taunt it.

73
00:05:04,172 --> 00:05:06,780
A friendly station lets you dock.

74
00:05:07,230 --> 00:05:11,578
And one thing it does not buy you: a fight.

75
00:05:12,028 --> 00:05:14,202
The cutter has no orders.

76
00:05:14,652 --> 00:05:16,391
It will sit there.

77
00:05:17,591 --> 00:05:18,591
Lint.

78
00:05:19,041 --> 00:05:21,215
A field I misspelled: caught.

79
00:05:21,665 --> 00:05:25,578
A landmark in the wrong section: caught. Now watch.

80
00:05:26,028 --> 00:05:29,507
Enemies, t s m. Clean. Side, braker. Clean.

81
00:05:29,957 --> 00:05:37,348
Lint does not check that a key after Enemies, or after Side, is a side that exists.

82
00:05:37,798 --> 00:05:47,363
In the game those two mistakes look the same: the cutter reads unknown, forever, and Comms has nothing to say to it.

83
00:05:47,813 --> 00:05:51,291
So for this lecture, clean is not enough.

84
00:05:51,741 --> 00:06:00,437
Read the three key words by eye: the one in the heading, the one after Side, the one after Enemies.

85
00:06:01,637 --> 00:06:02,637
The yard.

86
00:06:03,087 --> 00:06:06,565
Unknown, until the scan is done. Green. Guild.

87
00:06:07,015 --> 00:06:08,320
A friendly station.

88
00:06:08,770 --> 00:06:10,074
Comms: hail them.

89
00:06:10,524 --> 00:06:11,828
Full docking privileges.

90
00:06:12,278 --> 00:06:14,017
And Helm can dock.

91
00:06:14,467 --> 00:06:17,076
Now the other one. Red. Breaker.

92
00:06:17,526 --> 00:06:20,570
Enemy vessel, exercise caution. Hail. Go away.

93
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:25,367
And it sits there: enemies, and no fight. Last thing.

94
00:06:25,817 --> 00:06:28,426
The log, to the yard. Nothing.

95
00:06:28,876 --> 00:06:30,615
To DS 1. Home.

96
00:06:31,815 --> 00:06:35,728
Write a faction of your own, with one ship.

97
00:06:36,178 --> 00:06:40,091
Say nothing about it, and Science calls it unknown.

98
00:06:40,541 --> 00:06:44,889
Give it a scan record, and it has a name.

99
00:06:45,339 --> 00:06:50,991
Make it an enemy, then a friend, and watch the name change color.

100
00:06:51,441 --> 00:06:54,920
Next time: the people who fly these ships.
